JavaScript implementation uses the MetroFuse plugin SDK, no embedded browser or Node APIs.
Features: Spotify browser/cookie login and authenticated desktop fallback, personalized
Pathfinder Home, REST fallback shelves, search, album/artist/playlist detail, account
library pagination, likes, matched metadata, Canvas and color lyrics. Artist metadata
includes biography, related artists, releases, playlists, concerts and merchandise
when present in the service response. Queue preserves Web Player order and duplicates.
History and host upcoming-queue replacement are opt-in; account changes close sockets
and invalidate in-flight operations. No Spotify audio decoder/DRM bypass is provided.

Service endpoints and persisted GraphQL hashes can change. Home Casita fallback
is not implemented. Library uses GraphQL first with Spotify REST fallback. Tests use
protocol-shaped fixtures; real account authentication, queue and history require live
validation. Exact queue is returned only from Spotify Web Player state, never a fake
recommendation list. History reflects observed host playback, not manufactured streams.
